hadiths[3]{hadithnumber,text}:
"27962","Abd al-Aziz ibn Abd al-Samad al-Ammi Abu Abd al-Samad narrated to us: Mansur narrated to us, from Mujahid, from a freedman of Ibn al-Zubayr called Yusuf ibn al-Zubayr, or al-Zubayr ibn Yusuf, from Ibn al-Zubayr, from Sawdah bint Zamah, she said: A man came to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and said: My father is a very old man, unable to perform Hajj. He said: What think you, had your father a debt, and you paid it for him, would it be accepted from you. He said: Yes. He, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Then Allah is more merciful; perform Hajj for your father."
"27963","Ibn Numayr narrated to us, from Ismail, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, from Sawdah, the wife of the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, she said: A sheep of ours died, so we tanned its skin, and we continued to make nabidh therein until it became a worn-out waterskin."
"27964","Aswad ibn Amir narrated to us: Israil narrated to us, from Mansur, from Mujahid, from a freedman of the family of al-Zubayr, he said: The daughter of Zamah said: I came to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and said: My father Zamah died and left a concubine of his, and we used to suspect her with a man, and she gave birth, and her child came out resembling the man we suspected her with. He said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said to her: As for you, veil yourself from him, for he is not your brother; and to him is the inheritance."
